  </div>

  <p>
    None of this means these students cannot succeed in engineering. It means the specific branch or
    reason behind the choice may need a second look, and an adjacent path like design-heavy roles,
    business-facing technical work, or a completely different stream might fit better than picking
    engineering by default.
  </p>

  <h2 id="checkpoint">Use The 4-Checkpoint Protocol before you commit to a branch</h2>

  <p>
    A single salary figure or a relative's opinion cannot tell you whether this fits your specific
    situation. The 4-Checkpoint Protocol narrows the decision to what actually matters for you.
  </p>

